 let's get into the new  inch 5k imac which starts at the same  base price of 17.99  except that we now get intel's latest  10gen chips on every configuration  and now you can get up to a 3.6  gigahertz  10 core i9 processor which is going to  be insane  previously the best choice was an 8 core  i9  and based on apple's performance charts  this new cpu is much more powerful  than the old acor as far as the design  it hasn't changed which is a bit  disappointing  but honestly the internal changes are  huge this year  and as far as the display it's basically  staying unchanged  except that you now have an option to  pay for the nano texture glass  which apple offered on their 6k pro  display xdr  which basically turns it into a high  quality matte display  without using a film that ruins the  colors and the contrast  you can now configure the ram up to 128  gigs  from apple for a massive 2600  but we do not recommend doing so because  you can buy four sticks of that ram that  we link to down below  and you'll get 128 gigs for only around  four hundred and sixty-five dollars  instead of two thousand  six hundred dollars you can now also  configure up to a massive  eight terabyte ssd which is a huge  difference  coming from the previous maximum of 2  terabytes  now there are three major features that  matter the most to  us as video editors and one of them is  the new graphics  the previous base 5k imac came with the  radeon pro 570x gpu  and the new one comes with the radeon  pro 5300  which is based on amd's new navi  graphics architecture which has a number  of advantages  the previous best gpu was the vega 48  and you can now get up to a 5700 xt  which is our favorite graphics card to  use in an egpu setup  because it's just so dang fast but this  isn't like  any other 5700 xt this one is the only  one  that comes with 16 gigs of vram which  you can't get on a pc  this is going to be a really big deal  for anybody doing graphics rendering  work  and finally the new 